## Codebase navigation — Sourcetrail code-graph + grep

AGENTS.md § Semantic codebase search says *navigate by meaning + exact
call-graph before raw text-search*. On Claude Code the concrete tools are the
**Sourcetrail code-graph index** (exact call-graph / definition facts from a
prebuilt libclang SQLite graph) and `Grep`/`Glob` (literal/symbol sweeps).

### Sourcetrail — exact navigation facts
`tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py` queries a prebuilt symbol graph of the C++ tree
for facts grep cannot answer — who *calls* a function (not who *mentions* it),
the definition site, class members, inheritance:

```bash
python tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py callers <sym>   # functions that call <sym> (caller @ call-site)
python tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py callees <sym>   # functions <sym> calls
python tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py def <sym>       # definition site → file:line
python tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py refs <sym>      # every reference/use
python tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py members <Type>  # members of a class/struct/namespace
python tools/sourcetrail/st_query.py name <substr>   # qualified names containing <substr>
```

Name match is a case-insensitive suffix on the qualified name (`send`,
`JiraClient::send`, fully-qualified all resolve). Full subcommand table,
re-indexing steps, and limits: [`tools/sourcetrail/README.md`](../tools/sourcetrail/README.md).
The `.srctrldb` index is git-ignored, machine-local, and a snapshot — rebuild
after large code changes (README § Re-indexing). If it is absent/stale, fall
back to grep.

### Grep / Glob — literal & exhaustive sweeps
Use `Grep`/`Glob` for exhaustive literal/symbol inventories and mechanical
rename sweeps (every occurrence must be found — graph queries are not
exhaustive), and as the fallback when the Sourcetrail index is unavailable.

### Subagent / Explore / Plan mode
- Subagents may call `st_query.py` and grep directly — pass the task description.
- Prefer a targeted `st_query.py` call over spawning Agent(Explore) for a
  "who calls X / where is X" question; reserve Explore for broad fan-out.